 '[{"text": "21 and 13", "feedback": "Correct. Adding x + y = 34 and x − y = 8 gives 2x = 42, so x = 21, and y = 34 − 21 = 13."}, {"text": "17 and 17", "feedback": "This splits the sum evenly, but that ignores the second condition — the two numbers also need to differ by 8."}, {"text": "26 and 8", "feedback": "8 is the difference itself, not one of the two numbers — solve the system rather than reusing a given value directly."}, {"text": "22 and 12", "feedback": "Close, but these don''t quite satisfy both conditions — recheck 2x = 34 + 8 before dividing by 2."}]'::jsonb,
 'system-word-problem-solve'),
('MPM2D', 'linear-systems', 'linear-system-applications', 11, 'Medium',
 'Twice one number plus a second number is 19. The first number minus the second is 2. Find both numbers.', 2,
