 '[{"text": "7.0", "feedback": "Recheck the midpoint of BC first — it isn''t (7, 0); average both the x- and y-coordinates of B and C."}, {"text": "8.0", "feedback": "This looks like just the y-coordinate of C was used — find the actual midpoint of BC first, then its distance from A."}, {"text": "8.1", "feedback": "Correct. The midpoint of BC is ((10+4)÷2, (0+8)÷2) = (7, 4), and the distance from A(0,0) to (7,4) is √(7²+4²) = √65 ≈ 8.1."}, {"text": "11.0", "feedback": "This is close to BC''s own length, not the median''s — the median runs from A to BC''s midpoint, not along BC itself."}]'::jsonb,
