 'A parabola opens downward, is narrower than y = x², and has vertex (-2, 5). Which of these could be its equation?', 1,
 '[{"text": "y = (x + 2)² + 5", "feedback": "This opens upward (positive coefficient) — the parabola needs to open downward, so the coefficient must be negative."}, {"text": "y = -3(x + 2)² + 5", "feedback": "Correct. The vertex (-2, 5) matches, the coefficient -3 is negative (opens downward), and |-3| > 1 makes it narrower than y = x²."}, {"text": "y = -0.5(x + 2)² + 5", "feedback": "The vertex and downward-opening direction are both right, but |-0.5| < 1 makes this wider than y = x², not narrower."}, {"text": "y = -3(x - 2)² + 5", "feedback": "The sign inside the bracket is off — a vertex at x = -2 needs (x + 2), not (x - 2)."}]'::jsonb,
