('MPM2D', 'quadratic-relations', 'expanding-and-simplifying', 11, 'Medium',
 'Expand and simplify: (x + 5)(3x - 2).', 3,
 '[{"text": "3x² - 10", "feedback": "This multiplies only the first and last terms and skips the two cross terms entirely."}, {"text": "3x² - 7x - 10", "feedback": "The sign on the middle term is flipped — recompute -2x + 15x, which is positive."}, {"text": "3x² + 13x + 10", "feedback": "The sign on the constant term is off — recheck (5)(-2)."}, {"text": "3x² + 13x - 10", "feedback": "Correct. (x)(3x)+(x)(-2)+(5)(3x)+(5)(-2) = 3x²-2x+15x-10 = 3x²+13x-10."}]'::jsonb,
 'binomial-expansion-leading-coefficient'),
('MPM2D', 'quadratic-relations', 'expanding-and-simplifying', 12, 'Medium',
 'Expand and simplify: (2x + 3)(2x - 3).', 0,
 '[{"text": "4x² - 9", "feedback": "Correct. This is a difference of squares: (2x)² - 3² = 4x² - 9 — the two middle terms cancel out."}, {"text": "4x² + 9", "feedback": "The sign on the constant term is off — for (a+b)(a−b), the result is a²−b², not a²+b²."}, {"text": "4x² - 12x - 9", "feedback": "This is a difference of squares — the two middle cross terms (6x and −6x) actually cancel each other out."}, {"text": "2x² - 9", "feedback": "The x² coefficient is off — (2x)(2x) = 4x², not 2x²."}]'::jsonb,
 'difference-of-squares'),
('MPM2D', 'quadratic-relations', 'expanding-and-simplifying', 13, 'Challenge',
 'Expand and simplify: (x + 3)² + (x - 3)².', 1,
 '[{"text": "2x² - 18", "feedback": "The sign on the constant is off — expanding both squares and adding, the +9 and +9 (not -9) combine."}, {"text": "2x² + 18", "feedback": "Correct. (x+3)² = x²+6x+9 and (x-3)² = x²-6x+9; adding gives 2x²+18, since the 6x and -6x terms cancel."}, {"text": "2x² + 6x + 18", "feedback": "The two middle terms (6x and -6x from the two squares) actually cancel out completely when added together."}, {"text": "x² + 18", "feedback": "Both squared terms (x² from each expansion) need to be added together, giving 2x², not just x²."}]'::jsonb,
 'expand-add-two-squares'),
('MPM2D', 'quadratic-relations', 'expanding-and-simplifying', 14, 'Challenge',
 'Expand and simplify: (2x - 1)² - (x + 1)².', 3,
 '[{"text": "x² - 6x", "feedback": "The x² terms from each expansion (4x² and x²) should subtract to 3x², not 1x² — recheck that subtraction."}, {"text": "3x² - 2x", "feedback": "Recheck the middle term: combining -4x and -2x (with the second one''s sign flipped by the subtraction) gives -6x, not -2x."}, {"text": "3x² + 2x - 2", "feedback": "The constant terms don''t combine to -2 here — recheck 1 - 1 from the two expansions."}, {"text": "3x² - 6x", "feedback": "Correct. (2x-1)² = 4x²-4x+1 and (x+1)² = x²+2x+1; subtracting gives (4x²-4x+1)-(x²+2x+1) = 3x²-6x, since the constants (1 and 1) cancel."}]'::jsonb,
 'expand-subtract-two-squares'),
('MPM2D', 'quadratic-relations', 'expanding-and-simplifying', 15, 'Challenge',
 'Expand and simplify: (x + 5)(x - 5) + 2x².', 2,
 '[{"text": "x² - 25", "feedback": "This only expands the difference-of-squares part and forgets to add the extra 2x² term."}, {"text": "3x² - 10", "feedback": "This treats (x+5)(x-5) as if it produced a middle term of its own — it''s a difference of squares, x²-25, with no x term."}, {"text": "3x² - 25", "feedback": "Correct. (x+5)(x-5) = x²-25 (a difference of squares), and adding 2x² gives x²-25+2x² = 3x²-25."}, {"text": "2x² - 25", "feedback": "The x² term from (x+5)(x-5) itself needs to be added to the extra 2x² as well, giving 3x², not just 2x²."}]'::jsonb,
