('MPM2D', 'quadratic-relations', 'completing-the-square', 9, 'Medium',
 'Write y = x² + 4x + 7 in vertex form by completing the square.', 0,
 '[{"text": "y = (x + 2)² + 3", "feedback": "Correct. Half of 4 is 2, and (x+2)² expands to x²+4x+4, so the original +7 becomes 7−4 = 3 once that extra 4 is removed."}, {"text": "y = (x - 2)² + 3", "feedback": "The sign inside the bracket is flipped — since the original term is +4x, the bracket should be (x + 2), not (x − 2)."}, {"text": "y = (x + 2)² + 7", "feedback": "The bracket is right, but the constant wasn''t adjusted — adding (x+2)²''s extra +4 means 7 must be reduced by 4."}, {"text": "y = (x + 4)² + 3", "feedback": "The bracket should use half of the x-coefficient (4÷2=2), not the full coefficient itself."}]'::jsonb,
 'completing-square-vertex-form'),
