 'quadratic-formula-basic-solve'),
('MPM2D', 'quadratic-relations', 'quadratic-formula', 10, 'Medium',
 'Use the quadratic formula to solve x² + 2x - 8 = 0.', 1,
 '[{"text": "x = 4 and x = -2", "feedback": "The two roots are swapped — recheck (-b ± √(b²-4ac)) ÷ 2a carefully, keeping the ± signs matched to the right roots."}, {"text": "x = 2 and x = -4", "feedback": "Correct. With a=1, b=2, c=-8: the discriminant is 4+32=36, so x = (-2 ± 6) ÷ 2, giving x = 2 or x = -4."}, {"text": "x = 8 and x = -1", "feedback": "These don''t satisfy the original equation — recompute the discriminant: 2²-4(1)(-8) = 36, then apply the formula directly."}, {"text": "x = -2 and x = 4", "feedback": "Check the sign of the first root — substituting x = -2 into x²+2x-8 doesn''t give 0."}]'::jsonb,
 'quadratic-formula-basic-solve'),
('MPM2D', 'quadratic-relations', 'quadratic-formula', 11, 'Medium',
 'Use the quadratic formula to solve 2x² + x - 6 = 0.', 2,
