 'Use the quadratic formula to solve x² - 4x - 21 = 0.', 0,
 '[{"text": "x = 7 and x = -3", "feedback": "Correct. With a=1, b=-4, c=-21: the discriminant is 16+84=100, so x = (4 ± 10) ÷ 2, giving x = 7 or x = -3."}, {"text": "x = -7 and x = 3", "feedback": "The signs are flipped — recheck (-b ± √(b²-4ac)) ÷ 2a with b = -4, which makes -b positive."}, {"text": "x = 4 and x = 21", "feedback": "These reuse the equation''s own coefficients directly instead of applying the quadratic formula."}, {"text": "x = 5 and x = -1", "feedback": "These don''t satisfy the original equation — recompute the discriminant: (-4)²-4(1)(-21) = 100, then apply the formula directly."}]'::jsonb,
