('MPM2D', 'quadratic-relations', 'quadratic-formula', 13, 'Challenge',
 'Use the quadratic formula to solve x² + 3x - 2 = 0. Round your answers to one decimal place.', 1,
 '[{"text": "x ≈ 1.2 or x ≈ -4.2", "feedback": "Recheck the discriminant: b²-4ac = 3²-4(1)(-2) = 17, not a value leading to these roots."}, {"text": "x ≈ 0.6 or x ≈ -3.6", "feedback": "Correct. With a=1, b=3, c=-2: the discriminant is 9+8=17, so x = (-3 ± √17) ÷ 2, giving x ≈ 0.6 or x ≈ -3.6."}, {"text": "x = 2 or x = -1", "feedback": "These look like factoring-style \"nice\" answers, but this equation''s discriminant (17) isn''t a perfect square, so the true solutions are irrational."}, {"text": "x ≈ 3.6 or x ≈ -0.6", "feedback": "The signs are flipped from the correct decimal values — recheck (-3 ± √17) ÷ 2 carefully."}]'::jsonb,
 'quadratic-formula-decimal-rounding'),
('MPM2D', 'quadratic-relations', 'quadratic-formula', 14, 'Challenge',
 'Use the quadratic formula to solve x² - 5x + 2 = 0. Round your answers to one decimal place.', 2,
 '[{"text": "x ≈ 5.0 or x ≈ 2.0", "feedback": "These reuse the equation''s own coefficients directly instead of applying the quadratic formula."}, {"text": "x ≈ -4.6 or x ≈ -0.4", "feedback": "The signs are flipped from the correct decimal values — recheck (5 ± √17) ÷ 2 carefully, since -b = 5 here."}, {"text": "x ≈ 4.6 or x ≈ 0.4", "feedback": "Correct. With a=1, b=-5, c=2: the discriminant is 25-8=17, so x = (5 ± √17) ÷ 2, giving x ≈ 4.6 or x ≈ 0.4."}, {"text": "x = 4 or x = 1", "feedback": "These look like factoring-style \"nice\" answers, but this equation''s discriminant (17) isn''t a perfect square, so the true solutions are irrational."}]'::jsonb,
 'quadratic-formula-decimal-rounding'),
('MPM2D', 'quadratic-relations', 'quadratic-formula', 15, 'Challenge',
 'What can you conclude about the solutions of 2x² - 3x + 5 = 0, without fully solving it?', 3,
 '[{"text": "It has two different real solutions, since the discriminant is positive", "feedback": "Recompute the discriminant: (-3)²-4(2)(5) = 9-40 = -31, which is negative, not positive."}, {"text": "It has exactly one real solution, since the discriminant is zero", "feedback": "Recompute the discriminant: (-3)²-4(2)(5) = 9-40 = -31 — that isn''t zero."}, {"text": "It has two equal real solutions", "feedback": "Two equal real solutions would need a discriminant of exactly zero — this one comes out negative instead."}, {"text": "It has no real solutions, since the discriminant is negative", "feedback": "Correct. The discriminant is (-3)²-4(2)(5) = 9-40 = -31, which is negative — a negative discriminant means there are no real solutions."}]'::jsonb,
 'discriminant-determines-number-of-solutions'),
