 '[{"text": "k = 9", "feedback": "Correct. Exactly one real solution means the discriminant is zero: 6²-4(1)(k) = 0, so 36 = 4k, giving k = 9."}, {"text": "k = 6", "feedback": "This reuses the coefficient of x directly — solve 36-4k=0 for k instead."}, {"text": "k = 36", "feedback": "This is the value of b² itself, before solving 36-4k=0 for k — one more step is needed."}, {"text": "k = 0", "feedback": "Setting k=0 gives a discriminant of 36-0=36, which is positive, not zero — that would give two real solutions, not one."}]'::jsonb,
