 '[{"text": "x = 2 and x = -1.5", "feedback": "These don''t satisfy the original equation — recompute the discriminant: (-7)²-4(3)(-6) = 121, then apply the formula directly."}, {"text": "x = -3 and x = 2/3", "feedback": "The signs are flipped from the correct solutions — recheck (-b ± √(b²-4ac)) ÷ 2a with b = -7, which makes -b positive."}, {"text": "x = 3 and x = -2/3", "feedback": "Correct. With a=3, b=-7, c=-6: the discriminant is 49+72=121=11², so x = (7 ± 11) ÷ 6, giving x = 3 or x = -2/3."}, {"text": "x = 7 and x = 6", "feedback": "These reuse the equation''s own coefficients directly instead of applying the quadratic formula."}]'::jsonb,
