 '[{"text": "EF = 7", "feedback": "This reuses BC''s length directly — the similarity ratio between the two triangles needs to be applied to it first."}, {"text": "EF = 21", "feedback": "Correct. The scale factor from triangle ABC to DEF is DE ÷ AB = 15 ÷ 5 = 3, so EF = BC × 3 = 7 × 3 = 21."}, {"text": "EF = 5", "feedback": "This reuses AB''s length instead of BC''s, and doesn''t apply the scale factor between the triangles."}, {"text": "EF = 17", "feedback": "This adds 15 and 7 minus 5 rather than applying the scale factor DE ÷ AB to BC."}]'::jsonb,
