 '[{"text": "50/18, since areas scale the same as sides", "feedback": "Area scales with the *square* of the linear scale factor, not the same ratio — take a square root to undo that."}, {"text": "32, since areas subtract to find the scale factor", "feedback": "Areas of similar shapes relate by a squared ratio, not a simple difference — divide the areas, then take a square root."}, {"text": "25/9", "feedback": "This is the ratio of the areas (50÷18 simplified) — the linear scale factor is the square root of this ratio, not the ratio itself."}, {"text": "5/3", "feedback": "Correct. The ratio of the areas is 50÷18 = 25/9; since area scales with the square of the linear scale factor, taking the square root of 25/9 gives 5/3."}]'::jsonb,
