 '[{"text": "13.3 m", "feedback": "This adds instead of using the ratio — set up a proportion between the pole heights and their shadow lengths instead."}, {"text": "6 m", "feedback": "Check this against the proportion 3/4 = h/10 — it doesn''t satisfy that equation."}, {"text": "7.5 m", "feedback": "Correct. Similar triangles give the proportion (short pole height)/(short shadow) = (tall pole height)/(tall shadow): 3/4 = h/10, so h = 3×10÷4 = 7.5 m."}, {"text": "13.3 m, using 10×4÷3", "feedback": "This inverts the proportion — set up 3/4 = h/10 (height over shadow, matched consistently) rather than swapping which values divide which."}]'::jsonb,
