 '[{"text": "18/25", "feedback": "This subtracts 7 from 25 directly instead of using the Pythagorean theorem to find the missing side."}, {"text": "7/25", "feedback": "This reuses sine''s value for cosine — cosine compares a different pair of sides than sine does."}, {"text": "25/24", "feedback": "This has the ratio upside down, and 25 isn''t the adjacent side — cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse, and the hypotenuse here is 25."}, {"text": "24/25", "feedback": "Correct. With opposite = 7 and hypotenuse = 25, the adjacent side is √(25²−7²) = √576 = 24 (a 7-24-25 triangle), so cos θ = adjacent ÷ hypotenuse = 24/25."}]'::jsonb,
